I read the diff against the task and checked the call sites. The token is generated and hashed in `store.go`, the plaintext is returned only from `CreateInvite`, and `team.go:149` puts `inv.Token` into the email link. Accept uses the hash and the service clock (`team.go:178`), and the listing uses `PendingInvites` with `expires_at`. Re-invite revokes older pending invites case-insensitively, and the snapshot keeps only hashes. I found no correctness, security or requirement gaps.

Optional note, not a reason to revise: a snapshot written before this change has no `expires_at` and no token hashes. Restoring it gives pending invites a zero `ExpiresAt`, so they count as expired. Their plaintext tokens were not persisted before either, so they were not usable anyway. If old snapshots need to be restored, a migration note would help.

